One issue: `native_get_round_gamemode_name` uses `set_string(1, "нет режима", iLen)` — set_string(param, string, len) copies to the caller's buffer. But there's a subtlety: `set_string(1, source, iLen)` where iLen comes from `get_param(2)` — the caller passes `dest[]` and `len`. The native writes at most iLen chars into the dest buffer referenced by param 1. Since the caller guarantees len = charsmax(dest), this is safe. ✓

Also `ResetStats(get_param(1))` — if a caller passes an invalid id like 500, ResetStats(500) → ClearPlayerStats(500) → g_iRoundStats[500] → out of bounds at runtime! `native_reset_user_stats(id = 0)` — id 0 means all, otherwise a player index. Add bounds validation:

```pawn
public native_reset_user_stats(plugin, params)
{
	new id = get_param(1);
	if (id != 0 && (id < 1 || id > MAX_PLAYERS))
		return 0;
	ResetStats(id);
	return 1;
}
```

